answer_vi:
Go không có try/catch/throw. Errors là values, check lỗi ngay sau khi gọi. Explicit > implicit.
```go
// Hàm trả (result, error)
func readFile(path string) ([]byte, error) {
    data, err := os.ReadFile(path)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("readFile %s: %w", path, err)
    }
    return data, nil
}

// Xử lý lỗi tại nơi gọi
data, err := readFile("config.json")
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}

// Custom error
var ErrNotFound = errors.New("not found")

// Wrap và unwrap error
err := fmt.Errorf("service layer: %w", ErrNotFound)
errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) // true
```
`errors.Is()`, `errors.As()` để check error chain.

answer_en:
Go has no try/catch/throw. Errors are values; check them immediately after the call. Explicit over implicit.
```go
// Function returns (result, error)
func readFile(path string) ([]byte, error) {
    data, err := os.ReadFile(path)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("readFile %s: %w", path, err)
    }
    return data, nil
}

// Handle error at the call site
data, err := readFile("config.json")
if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
}

// Custom sentinel error
var ErrNotFound = errors.New("not found")

// Wrap and unwrap errors
err := fmt.Errorf("service layer: %w", ErrNotFound)
errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) // true
```
Use `errors.Is()` and `errors.As()` to inspect the error chain.
